---
title: Directory
teaser: "Every part of this site on one page: the writing, the projects, and the machinery."
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /directory/
---
{#
  The human counterpart to /sitemap.xml.

  Deliberately a map of PLACES, not of entries. /all/ and /archive/ already
  list all ~100 entries, and a third list of the same titles would be a third
  thing to scroll rather than a way to see the shape of the site. This page
  answers "what is here?"; those answer "what has been published?".

  Counts come from the collections, so a new section or topic appears here
  without anyone remembering to add it. The one hand-maintained part is the
  grouping, because what belongs next to what is an editorial judgement.
#}
<section>
  <h1 class="kh-font-headline kh-font-headline--display kh-text-heading--1">{{ title }}</h1>

  <div class="kh-content">
    <p>Everything on this site, grouped by what it is for. Counted at build
    time, so it cannot drift out of date. If you want the entries themselves
    rather than the places they live, <a href="/all/">All writing</a> lists
    them newest first and <a href="/archive/">the archive</a> lists them by
    month.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="kh-section-head kh-u-margin__top--1200">
    <h2 id="writing" class="kh-text-heading--2"><span class="kh-section-number">1.0</span>Writing</h2>
    <span class="kh-meta">{{ collections.allContent | length }} entries in total</span>
  </div>
  <div class="kh-panel">
    <div class="kh-panel__row" style="--kh-panel-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr">
      <div class="kh-panel__cell">
        <span class="kh-panel__label">Blog</span>
        <a href="/blog/">Longer pieces &amp; notes</a>
        <span class="kh-meta kh-u-margin__top--200">{{ collections.blogPosts | length }} entries</span>
      </div>
      <div class="kh-panel__cell">
        <span class="kh-panel__label">Digesting</span>
        <a href="/digesting/">Bookmarks &amp; reading</a>
        <span class="kh-meta kh-u-margin__top--200">{{ collections.digesting | published | length }} entries</span>
      </div>
      <div class="kh-panel__cell">
        <span class="kh-panel__label">Work</span>
        <a href="/work/">Impact stories</a>
        <span class="kh-meta kh-u-margin__top--200">{{ collections.impactStories | length }} entries</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="kh-panel__row" style="--kh-panel-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr">
      <div class="kh-panel__cell">
        <span class="kh-panel__label">Everything</span>
        <a href="/all/">All writing</a>
        <span class="kh-meta kh-u-margin__top--200">newest first, paginated</span>
      </div>
      <div class="kh-panel__cell">
        <span class="kh-panel__label">By month</span>
        <a href="/archive/">Archive</a>
        <span class="kh-meta kh-u-margin__top--200">one dense page</span>
      </div>
      <div class="kh-panel__cell">
        <span class="kh-panel__label">By subject</span>
        <a href="#subjects">Topics</a>
        <span class="kh-meta kh-u-margin__top--200">{{ collections.topics | length }} topics</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {#- This absorbed a /topics/ index page that briefly existed alongside it.
      Both listed the same 31 topics and only /topics/ carried the sparklines,
      so the flat chip list that used to sit here was the poorer of two copies.
      The table moved in and that page went away before either shipped, which
      is why there is no redirect for it -- the URL was never live.

      The child pages at /topics/<slug>/ are unaffected and still exist; this
      is their index. -#}
  <div class="kh-section-head kh-u-margin__top--1200">
    <h2 id="subjects" class="kh-text-heading--2"><span class="kh-section-number">2.0</span>Subjects</h2>
    <span class="kh-meta">{{ collections.topics | length }} topics &middot; by entry count</span>
  </div>

  <div class="kh-content">
    <p>The subject vocabulary is deliberately small. It was consolidated from 158
    ad-hoc terms, of which 116 appeared exactly once, into a controlled set. Only
    topics carrying three or more entries get a page here; anything thinner lives
    as detail after a <code>&gt;</code> on the entry itself.</p>
  </div>

  {#- Count is the encoding: the number is stated, and the bar is a length on a
      common scale, which is the most accurately read visual channel. No area,
      no font-size scaling, no cloud. -#}
  {#- One shared peak across all rows, so heights are comparable. -#}
  {%- set peak = 0 %}
  {%- for t in collections.topics %}{% if t.peak > peak %}{% set peak = t.peak %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
  <div class="kh-table-scroll">
    <table class="kh-table--spec kh-topic-index">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">By year <span class="kh-spark__axis">{{ collections.topics[0].firstYear }}&ndash;{{ collections.topics[0].lastYear }}</span></th>
          <th scope="col">Entries</th>
          <th scope="col">Topic</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {%- for t in collections.topics %}
        <tr>
          <td class="kh-topic-index__spark">
            {% topicSparkline t.perYear, peak, t.topic %}
          </td>
          <td class="kh-topic-index__count">{{ t.count }}</td>
          <td><a href="/topics/{{ t.slug }}/">{{ t.topic }}</a></td>
        </tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="kh-section-head kh-u-margin__top--1200">
    <h2 id="making" class="kh-text-heading--2"><span class="kh-section-number">3.0</span>Making</h2>
    <span class="kh-meta">{{ garage | length }} projects</span>
  </div>
  <div class="kh-panel">
    <div class="kh-panel__row" style="--kh-panel-columns: 1fr">
      <div class="kh-panel__cell">
        <span class="kh-panel__label">Index</span>
        <a href="/garage/">The garage</a>
        <span class="kh-meta kh-u-margin__top--200">side projects, utilities and experiments</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    {%- for project in garage %}
    <div class="kh-panel__row" style="--kh-panel-columns: 1fr">
      <div class="kh-panel__cell">
        <span class="kh-panel__label">{{ project.status }}</span>
        <a href="{{ project.path }}">{{ project.name }}</a>
        <span class="kh-meta kh-u-margin__top--200">{{ project.description }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>

  <div class="kh-section-head kh-u-margin__top--1200">
    <h2 id="about" class="kh-text-heading--2"><span class="kh-section-number">4.0</span>About</h2>
    <span class="kh-meta">Who and how</span>
  </div>
  <div class="kh-panel">
    <div class="kh-panel__row" style="--kh-panel-columns: 1fr 1fr">
      <div class="kh-panel__cell">
        <span class="kh-panel__label">Start</span>
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span class="kh-meta kh-u-margin__top--200">the short version</span>
      </div>
      <div class="kh-panel__cell">
        <span class="kh-panel__label">Long form</span>
        <a href="/cv/">CV</a>
        <span class="kh-meta kh-u-margin__top--200">roles, dates and evidence</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="kh-panel__row" style="--kh-panel-columns: 1fr 1fr">
      <div class="kh-panel__cell">
        <span class="kh-panel__label">How it is built</span>
        <a href="/colophon/">Colophon</a>
        <span class="kh-meta kh-u-margin__top--200">stack, type and credits</span>
      </div>
      <div class="kh-panel__cell">
        <span class="kh-panel__label">Slash page</span>
        <a href="/ai/">AI notes</a>
        <span class="kh-meta kh-u-margin__top--200">how AI is and is not used here</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kh-section-head kh-u-margin__top--1200">
    <h2 id="machinery" class="kh-text-heading--2"><span class="kh-section-number">5.0</span>Machinery</h2>
    <span class="kh-meta">Finding, measuring, feeds and small print</span>
  </div>
  <div class="kh-panel">
    <div class="kh-panel__row" style="--kh-panel-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr">
      <div class="kh-panel__cell">
        <span class="kh-panel__label">Find</span>
        <a href="/search/">Search</a>
        <span class="kh-meta kh-u-margin__top--200">keyword and semantic</span>
      </div>
      <div class="kh-panel__cell">
        <span class="kh-panel__label">Measure</span>
        <a href="/stats/">Stats</a>
        <span class="kh-meta kh-u-margin__top--200">the corpus, counted</span>
      </div>
      <div class="kh-panel__cell">
        <span class="kh-panel__label">Patterns</span>
        <a href="/style-guide/components/">Style guide</a>
        <span class="kh-meta kh-u-margin__top--200">components and editorial rules</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    {#- The lab had exactly one inbound link on the whole site -- a body-text
        mention inside a single post -- and was missing from this page, which
        opens by claiming to list everything. Both first-time-visitor reviews
        found it by accident or not at all. -#}
    <div class="kh-panel__row" style="--kh-panel-columns: 1fr">
      <div class="kh-panel__cell">
        <span class="kh-panel__label">Experiment</span>
        <a href="/stats/story-lab/">Corpus story lab</a>
        <span class="kh-meta kh-u-margin__top--200">several ways of reading the archive as data; experimental and deliberately rough</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="kh-panel__row" style="--kh-panel-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr">
      <div class="kh-panel__cell">
        <span class="kh-panel__label">Subscribe</span>
        <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>
        <span class="kh-meta kh-u-margin__top--200">the last ten entries</span>
      </div>
      <div class="kh-panel__cell">
        <span class="kh-panel__label">For machines</span>
        <a href="/sitemap.xml">sitemap.xml</a>
        <span class="kh-meta kh-u-margin__top--200">every indexable URL</span>
      </div>
      <div class="kh-panel__cell">
        <span class="kh-panel__label">Small print</span>
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> &middot; <a href="/impressum/">Impressum</a>
        <span class="kh-meta kh-u-margin__top--200">no tracking beyond counts</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
